This is the experimental source tree for QtMoko2.

The goal of QtMoko2 is to rewrite/port intersting applications
and tools from QtMoko to use Qt5 libraries as provided by Debian
Jessie.

This removes the dependency on compiling (and maintaining) QPE
and allows to run QtMoko on different devices and architectures
because it can much easier be recompiled.

It is planned to add debian packaging files so that the source
code and be distributed as debian source packages and the binaries
can be rebuilt on any Debian machine from scratch.

It should become easily possible to create a download.qtmoko.net
repository where all packages are provided so that a simple
addition to /etc/apt/sources.list.d allows to use standard
Debian installation tools.

At some stage in the future we should tree-rewrite the git
so that all other files above are removed and this directory
becomes the root of the git repo.

But for the initial experimentations it is better to have everything
grouped here.
